The forwarding rules of getty-bun.sh forward_to_powershell (GETTY_HOME conversion, failure lines, unchanged arguments, and the stdin rule: a non-tty character device gets an empty pipe, everything else exec) are checked on Linux only by a local, untracked script with a fake uname, cygpath and PowerShell under dash, bash and BusyBox sh. A regression in that branch passes Linux CI. Done: the same checks as a bun:test group in bootstrap/test that runs on Linux CI, with the README labels pointing at it. Found in the phase 1 round six review (k9).
